OL,3,APart of Antarctica named after former
OL,4,ABBC science correspondent
OL,5,
OL,6,FPart of Antarctica has been named after
OL,7,Fformer BBC science correspondent
OL,8,FJonathan Amos.
OL,10,FA stretch of water between Rothschild
OL,11,FIsland and Alexander Island in the west
OL,12,Fof the White Continent is now called
OL,13,Fthe Amos Channel.
OL,15,FAmos was given the honour for his
OL,16,F"exceptional and influential role in
OL,17,Fbringing Antarctic research to the
OL,18,Fforefront of public understanding"
OL,19,Fduring his 38-year career at BBC News,
OL,20,Fthe naming committee said.
OL,23,APub: 26-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,318,300,200,140,0,100
